* Print the first fifteen Fibonacci numbers on the on-line printer.
*
* WRS 753 is octal 1361: channel A, printer 0361. RCHA hands the channel a
* command list; IOCD moves one word and disconnects. TCOA spins until it does.

       ORG   200
START  AXT   15,1
       CLA   ZERO
       STO   A
       CLA   ONE
       STO   B

LOOP   CLA   B
       TSX   PUTNUM,2
       TSX   PRINT,2
       CLA   A
       ADD   B
       STO   C
       CLA   B
       STO   A
       CLA   C
       STO   B
       TIX   LOOP,1,1
       HTR   0

* Convert the accumulator to six BCD digits in LINE.
* Each pass divides by ten; the remainder is already in the bottom six bits of
* the accumulator, so LGR shifts it straight into the top character of the MQ.

PUTNUM STO   N
       CLA   ZERO
       STO   LINE
       AXT   6,4
PUTD   CLA   ZERO
       LDQ   N
       DVP   TEN
       STQ   N
       LDQ   LINE
       LGR   6
       STQ   LINE
       TIX   PUTD,4,1
       TRA   1,2

PRINT  WRS   753
       RCHA  PCMD
PWAIT  TCOA  PWAIT
       TRA   1,2

PCMD   IOCD  LINE,0,1
LINE   OCT   000000000000

ZERO   OCT   000000000000
ONE    OCT   000000000001
TEN    OCT   000000000012
A      OCT   000000000000
B      OCT   000000000000
C      OCT   000000000000
N      OCT   000000000000
       END   START
